  "question": {
    "text": "In a common emitter configuration, a transistor has $\\beta=50$ and input resistance $1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$. If the peak value of a.c. input is $0.01 \\mathrm{~V}$ then the peak value of collector current is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0.01 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.25 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$100 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$500 \\mu \\mathrm{A}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Hints: } \\beta=50 \\Rightarrow \\beta=\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{C}}}{\\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}} \\Rightarrow \\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\beta \\times \\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}\n$$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}=\\frac{0.01}{10^3}=10^{-2} \\times 10^{-3}=10^{-5} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{C}}=50 \\times 10^{-5}=500 \\times 10^{-6}=500 \\mu \\mathrm{A}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}